{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Big Argument"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Out on the Town"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Negative Questions To Encourage Agreement"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Negative questions have a different meaning than regular questions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use negative questions to confirm information you already know, like <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think ... ?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Negative questions can have two different meanings. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can ask a negative question for confirmation of a positive belief. <br/>You can ask a negative question for confirmation of a negative belief."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't you think it's wonderful to have a soulmate?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't you think that successful relationships are rare these days?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't you think you should branch out a little? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't you think that long distance relationships  are doomed?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present vs. Present Perfect vs. Simple Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<ol><li>You use the Simple Present to talk about things that are true and things that you do regularly in the present.</li><li>You use the Present Perfect for actions which started in the past and are still happening now OR for finished actions which have a connection to the present.</li><li>You use the Simple Past for past events or actions which have no connection to the present.</li></ol>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present</span> is used when the action is always true or happens regularly.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Of course I sound desperate! No one understands my passion for comics.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The time period IS the present and is true all the time.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect</span> is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In fact, most of my dates have been fiascos because of my passion for comics.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The time period goes up to the present.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span> is used when the time period HAS finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We got along so well. Of course, it wasn't meant to be.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The time period has finished.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heartwarming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "emotionally uplifting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your parents have been in love for 50 years. It's a heartwarming love story."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le01ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you 